---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro"
import PublicHeader from "@/components/public-header.astro"
import OfflineFooter from "@/components/offline-footer.astro"
import { APP_NAME } from "@/lib/site"

const lastUpdated = "November 14, 2026"

const sections = [
  {
    id: "scope",
    title: "1. Scope & Applicability",
    content: `This Privacy Policy outlines how ${APP_NAME} ("we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, protects, and discloses information when you use our website, public documentation, interactive playground, and our high-performance LLM routing gateway API. By accessing or using our services, you acknowledge and agree to the practices described herein.`,
  },
  {
    id: "data-we-collect",
    title: "2. Information We Collect",
    content: `We collect minimal operational data required to reliably route AI inferences and maintain user accounts:

• Account Information: When you create an account, we collect your email address and securely hashed authentication credentials.
• Telemetry & Routing Metadata: We record high-level operational metrics including latency, time-to-first-token (TTFT), model group names, upstream provider IDs, prompt token counts, and completion token counts.
• Credit & Transaction Records: We maintain persistent records of your account credit balance, token consumption calculations, and coupon redemptions for billing auditability.`,
  },
  {
    id: "zdr",
    title: "3. Request Tracing & Prompt Handling",
    content: `Request tracing is enabled by default for new accounts. You can turn it off in Account Settings to stop new trace recordings for your requests.

• Request Traces: When tracing is enabled, Gateway stores sanitized request payloads and provider attempt details, including model, latency, and reported token usage. These records are available in the Request Traces dashboard.
• Trace Retention: Saved traces follow the retention period configured by the gateway administrator.
• No Model Training: We never use, sell, or license customer prompt inputs or model outputs to train artificial intelligence models.`,
  },
  {
    id: "upstream-providers",
    title: "4. Third-Party AI Model Providers",
    content: `When you dispatch inference requests through Gateway, your prompts are forwarded to the upstream providers configured in your model groups (such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Vertex AI, Mistral, or custom endpoints). Upstream providers handle data according to their respective enterprise terms. Administrators have full autonomy to select and filter which providers receive traffic.`,
  },
  {
    id: "use-of-info",
    title: "5. How We Use Information",
    content: `We process data exclusively for the following operational purposes:

• Routing and executing your LLM inference requests.
• Calculating real-time credit consumption and enforcing rate limits.
• Monitoring uptime, mitigating DDoS attempts, and investigating service errors.
• Responding to support inquiries and ticket communications raised through our support desk.`,
  },
  {
    id: "data-sharing",
    title: "6. Information Sharing & Disclosure",
    content: `We never sell, rent, or trade your personal information or prompt contents to third parties or advertisers. We disclose data only under the following limited circumstances:

• Upstream Providers: As strictly necessary to transmit your request payload to the designated AI provider.
• Legal Compliance: In response to valid, legally binding court orders, search warrants, or statutory obligations.
• Security & Safety: When necessary to investigate severe security incidents, malicious exploits, or infrastructure abuse.`,
  },
  {
    id: "security",
    title: "7. Security & Encryption",
    content: `We enforce industry-standard security safeguards to protect your data:

• Secret Encryption: Provider API keys and sensitive credentials are encrypted using authenticated cryptography before being stored.
• API Key Hashing: Gateway API keys generated by users are hashed at rest using SHA-256; only the unrecoverable key prefix is displayed.
• Session Security: Authentication sessions rely on short-lived JWT access tokens and secure refresh token exchange.`,
  },
  {
    id: "user-rights",
    title: "8. User Rights & Account Controls",
    content: `You maintain complete control over your personal data:

• Access & Export: You can inspect all API keys, usage logs, trace payloads, and credit transactions via your dashboard.
• Instant Revocation: You can immediately revoke API keys and invalidate active sessions at any time.
• Tracing Toggles: You can enable or disable payload tracing and OpenTelemetry telemetry collection with a single click.
• Account Deletion: You can request complete deletion of your account and associated records by contacting our support desk.`,
  },
  {
    id: "contact",
    title: "9. Contact Information",
    content: `If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or our data handling practices, please contact our team via the Support Desk in your dashboard or visit /support.`,
  },
]
---

<Layout title={`Privacy Policy — ${APP_NAME}`}>
  <PublicHeader current="privacy" />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      {/* Header */}
      <div class="border-b border-border/60 pb-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
          Last Updated: {lastUpdated}
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          At {APP_NAME}, we take your data privacy and sovereignty seriously.
          This document explains our Zero Data Retention principles, how your AI
          inferences are routed, and the controls available to you.
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* Sections */}
      <div class="mt-10 space-y-12">
        {sections.map((sec) => (
          <section id={sec.id} class="scroll-mt-20">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground sm:text-xl">
              {sec.title}
            </h2>
            <div class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground whitespace-pre-line">
              {sec.content}
            </div>
          </section>
        ))}
      </div>

      {/* Support footer notice */}
      <div class="mt-16 rounded-2xl border border-border/80 bg-muted/20 p-6 text-center">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">
          Have questions about our data practices?
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
          Our engineering and security teams are available through the ticket
          support desk.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/support"
          class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-primary-foreground shadow-xs hover:bg-primary/90 transition-all"
        >
          Contact Support
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <OfflineFooter />
</Layout>
